# @intra/api — DDD bounded contexts

Six bounded contexts live under `src/contexts/`: `identity`, `organisation`, `library`,
`feedback360`, `reporting`, `notifications`. Each is a self-contained NestJS module.

## Layering — put new code in the right layer

```
contexts/<context>/
├── domain/                        *.domain.ts — plain classes, NO Nest/Prisma imports
├── application/
│   ├── ports/                     *.repository.port.ts — interfaces + injection tokens
│   ├── services/                  *.service.ts — use cases
│   ├── events/                    *.event.ts — domain event payloads
│   ├── listeners/                 *.listener.ts — in-process handlers
│   └── constants/
├── infrastructure/
│   ├── prisma-repositories/       concrete adapters implementing the ports
│   └── mappers/                   domain ↔ persistence
└── presentation/http/
    ├── controllers/               *.controller.ts — routes only, no business logic
    ├── dto/                       request DTOs with class-validator
    ├── models/                    response models
    └── mappers/                   domain ↔ HTTP
```

## Rules that are easy to break

- **Domain stays pure.** No `@nestjs/*`, no `@prisma/client`, no DTOs inside `domain/*.domain.ts`.
- **Services depend on ports, never on Prisma repositories.** Inject the token
  (`CYCLE_REPOSITORY`, `REPORT_REPOSITORY`, …); wire the concrete class in the module with
  `{ provide: TOKEN, useExisting: ConcreteRepo }`.
- **Controllers are thin.** Validate via DTO, call one service, map to a response model. Any branching
  on domain state belongs in the service.
- **Cross-context calls go through events, not direct imports.** Contexts communicate by
  choreography over `EventEmitter2`: emit an event, let the other context's listener react.
  `reporting` and `notifications` both listen to `cycle.stage.processed` and never import
  `feedback360` services. Do not introduce a direct service-to-service dependency across contexts.
- **Shared types live in `@intra/shared-kernel`**, not duplicated per context.

## Persistence

A single global `DatabaseModule` exposes one `PrismaService` (pg `Pool`, SSL in production).
Do not instantiate `PrismaClient` anywhere else.

## Path aliases

| Alias | Resolves to |
| --- | --- |
| `src/*` | `src/*` |
| `@intra/api` | `src/contexts` |
| `@intra/api/*` | `src/contexts/*` |

## Conventions

- Files are kebab-case with a role suffix: `cycle.service.ts`, `cycle.repository.port.ts`,
  `cycles.controller.ts`, `cycle-stage.listener.ts`, `cycle.domain.ts`.
- Controllers are plural (`CyclesController`), services singular (`CycleService`).
- Every endpoint carries the reusable Swagger decorators from `src/common/documentation/`.
  `apps/docs/api/openapi.json` is rewritten on each boot — do not hand-edit it.
- Read env only through the typed loaders in `src/config/`, never `process.env` inline.
